{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon ECS extends Amazon S3 Files support to the Amazon EC2 compute type - AWS","context":"Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) has expanded its support for Amazon S3 Files to tasks running on Amazon EC2 instances. This new feature allows users to connect containerized applications directly to data in Amazon S3 as a shared file system. Customers can now use standard file system semantics for file-based applications, AI agents, and data processing workloads without duplicating or staging files first. Amazon S3 Files, which is built on Amazon Elastic File System (EFS), delivers a shared file system that connects AWS compute resources directly with data in Amazon S3. This feature is available in all AWS commercial and AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. Customers can mount an Amazon S3 Files volume in their Amazon ECS tasks to read and write data in an S3 bucket using standard file system operations, with no application code changes required. Amazon S3 Files support was previously available for ECS tasks on AWS Fargate and ECS Managed Instances","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/amazon-ecs-s3-files-ec2/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"troubleshooting-efs","skill_description":"Diagnoses and resolves Amazon EFS issues including mount failures, NFS timeouts, permission errors, throughput problems, and burst credit exhaustion. Use when the user has an EFS file system that is not mounting, returning errors, performing slowly, or showing access denied.\n\n\nServices: efs, ec2, iam, kms, vpc, cloudwatch\nTasks: debug, troubleshoot, diagnose\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: storage\n*","skill_name":"troubleshooting-efs"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"launching-ec2-instance-with-best-practices","skill_description":"Launches an EC2 instance with secure, cost-efficient defaults including AMI selection, burstable instance sizing, least-privilege IAM roles, hardened security groups, encrypted EBS volumes, and comprehensive tagging. Use when deploying new EC2 instances following AWS best practices for security and cost optimization.\n\nServices: ec2, iam, vpc, cloudwatch, ebs\nTasks: deploy, configure, secure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: compute\n*","skill_name":"launching-ec2-instance-with-best-practices"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"setting-up-ec2-instance-profiles","skill_description":"Configures EC2 instances to securely call AWS services by creating and attaching IAM roles via instance profiles, eliminating hardcoded credentials. Use when an EC2 instance needs permissions to access AWS services like S3, DynamoDB, SQS, or CloudWatch through temporary credentials.\n\nServices: ec2, iam\nTasks: configure, secure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security\n*","skill_name":"setting-up-ec2-instance-profiles"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS docs for mounting EFS on EC2"}
